 "about": "Empires and their parts. 'empires': each sovereign power, the ruler names the border sources use for it ('rulers'), the map rows that are its core ('core') and the Wikipedia articles whose Wikidata items count as the empire when a membership is checked. 'memberships': dated memberships written for GeoHistory from general knowledge, each with the Wikipedia article that supports it. With 'rows' the membership applies to the named map territories and they are merged into the empire at world zoom (unless 'merge' is false); without 'rows' the part has no shape of its own in the sources and is only listed in the empire's panel. Further memberships are read from the border sources themselves (Cliopatria's member-of field; CShapes dependencies with the owners in dependency_owners.json or the sketch maps). 'verified' is set by tools/build_empires.py: true when the Wikidata item of the part names an item of the empire as its country, as what it is part of, or as its administrative parent.",
